under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0),
except where a feature's `source_licence` property says otherwise:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Attribution: "The Crossing reading map, Joe Burkinshaw", with a link to
https://github.com/JBurkinshaw/crossing-map

The terms of each source are listed per layer in data/README.md, and each
feature's `source_licence` property states the licence of its source.

Layers derived from the Copernicus DEM GLO-30 (the mountain glyphs, and the
hachures, contours and Oblique archives among the tiles) are also subject to
the Copernicus DEM licence, and anyone who reuses them is bound by it too.
The notice and disclaimer it requires are in data/README.md.

Quotations from The Crossing (the Spanish incipits of a few words each) are
© Cormac McCarthy, used for commentary, and are not licensed here.

The word lists in translations.json (`es_words`: a line's other Spanish
words, in alphabetical order, for search) come from the same text and are
not licensed here either.

The English translations of the novel's Spanish (the `en` field of
translations.json) are this site's own wording, but they translate
McCarthy's text, and the right to translate it is his. They are published
as a reading aid and commentary and are not licensed here. The rest of each
translation record (ids, pages, episodes, confidence, speakers and where
each line was spoken) is CC BY 4.0 like the other data.
